RISC-V: no sext.w for a LONG-to-INT cast whose operand is already in int32 range. Applied after perf-43; JIT only.
- genIntToIntCast sign-extends every LONG-to-INT cast (sext.w). New Lowering::IsInt64InInt32RangeInReg
  recognises LONG values whose register is already the sign extension of its low 32 bits (optionally in
  [0, INT32_MAX]): srli by 33..63, srai by 32..63, casts from INT (sign-extending, or zero-extending a
  value IsInt32NonNegativeInReg accepts), AND with an operand in [0, INT32_MAX], AND/OR/XOR/NOT of
  in-range operands, integer min/max of in-range operands and the Zbb bit counts. Such a cast is a copy,
  in codegen and in LSRA (which prefers the source register), and IsInt32NonNegativeInReg now also
  accepts a narrowing cast of a value in [0, INT32_MAX].
- "(int)(x >>> 32)", the high half of a hash fold, lowers to "x >> 32" (srai), which is that sign
  extension, so it also needs no sext.w.

